SCOPE OF THE ABOVE

The MIT licence above covers only what the 1.6 port added:

  - the C# in Source/ as it now stands, rebuilt from the source the original
    shipped: the null guards, the scoring loop factored into one method, and
    the reason string assembled from keyed strings instead of concatenated
    English
  - the fix to the trait-description append, which compared a translated
    degree label against an English word and so did nothing outside English
  - the ingredient filter override on the three jewellery items, which the
    inherited vanilla filter kept gold, silver, jade and obsidian out of
  - the English keyed strings and the French translation
  - the packaging and the documentation

IT DOES NOT COVER THE ORIGINAL MOD. The idea, the scoring thresholds, the mood
values, the three jewellery items and their stats, recipes and gates, the text
of the thoughts, and all forty-eight textures are DoctorStupid's work, reused
here:

  https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2903245563

DoctorStupid never declared a licence for them, so none is granted here and
none can be. They are redistributed under the usual practice for abandoned
mods - explicit credit, a link to the original, and removal on request.
About/Preview.png is theirs as it stands, and the textures are theirs byte for
byte, under their original paths.

If DoctorStupid asks for this to be taken down, it comes down. Immediately, and
without discussion.

ATTRIBUTION.md records what was taken and what was changed.
